// The CloudKit record a Mac saves when a turn a phone asked for ends, which
// the phone's subscription turns into a push (Lamp Bible/AgentRemote/AgentTurnPush.swift).
//
// Container iCloud.com.neus.lamp-bible, private database, default zone.
// Both apps use the Production environment (a Developer ID Mac can use no
// other). Production makes neither record types nor subscription types on
// first use: both are made in Development and deployed. Once, before the
// feature can work:
//
//  0. Sign the Mac with CloudKit for this container: an entitlements file
//     (icloud-services CloudKit, the container, and the same
//     icloud-container-environment build setting) and a Developer ID
//     provisioning profile carrying them. Until then the Mac writes no
//     records (it checks its own signature) and the phone's subscription
//     never fires: only the phone's own notifications, while Lamp runs.
//  1. Define the record type below in Development: in CloudKit Console
//     (Schema > Record Types, with the indexes marked QUERYABLE/SORTABLE
//     below), or with `xcrun cktool import-schema --environment development`.
//     Import replaces the Development schema whole, so use it only while the
//     container has no other record types.
//  2. Make the subscription type in Development: install the phone app built
//     with `LAMP_CLOUDKIT_ENVIRONMENT=Development` (the entitlement reads that
//     build setting; Production otherwise), signed in to iCloud, pair it
//     with a Mac, and turn on Settings > AI Features > Notify when a chat
//     finishes a turn. It saves the subscription Production will need.
//  3. In CloudKit Console, Deploy Schema Changes to Production.
//  4. Install the usual (Production) build again.
//
// recordName: turn.<deviceID>.<chatID>, written over by the chat's next turn.
// The alert's fields (title, subtitle, summary, body) are plain, as a push
// needs them: body holds the reply's opening only while the Mac's "Show the
// start of the reply" is on. A subscription is the account's: its pushes go
// to every device signed in to the same iCloud with Lamp.

DEFINE SCHEMA

    RECORD TYPE AgentTurnEnded (
        "___createTime" TIMESTAMP,
        "___createdBy"  REFERENCE,
        "___etag"       STRING,
        "___modTime"    TIMESTAMP,
        "___modifiedBy" REFERENCE,
        "___recordID"   REFERENCE QUERYABLE,
        deviceID        STRING QUERYABLE,
        chatID          STRING,
        kind            STRING,
        writingID       STRING,
        turnID          STRING,
        title           STRING,
        subtitle        STRING,
        outcome         STRING,
        summary         STRING,
        body            STRING,
        endedAt         TIMESTAMP QUERYABLE SORTABLE,
        GRANT WRITE TO "_creator",
        GRANT CREATE TO "_icloud",
        GRANT READ TO "_world"
    );
